ts 152% above its 10-year median.","Earnings yields are thin: an FCF yield of 1.6% (below the risk-free rate) and an EBIT/EV of 2.2% (vs the 8% bar).","The 21 covering analysts target $296 on average, 34% above the price, well away from the model's fair value."],"prof":["ROIC of 13% earns above the cost of capital of 9.9%, but the 3pp spread is short of the 7pp moat bar; returns have swung a lot from year to year (CV 1.25).","It converts 17% of revenue into free cash flow.","Earnings quality looks solid: a Piotroski score of 7/9 and cash conversion of 1.25x.","ROE of 28% comes mostly from margins and asset turnover rather than leverage (2.1x equity multiplier).","Operating margin is running 12pp above its own historical average, a peak-margin risk if conditions normalise.","It spends 0.9% of revenue on stock compensation."],"hlth":["Leverage is conservative at 1.0x net debt to EBITDA ($742.0M of cash against $3.0B of debt), with interest covered 11.6x.","Short-term liquidity is ample (current ratio 2.13).","Goodwill makes up 36% of assets, a soft asset exposed to impairment."],"growth":["Revenue has compounded at 13.4% over 3 years, 9.4% over 5 years and -9.6% over 10 years, so growth is accelerating, and it has been lumpy (year-to-year swings of 22%).","At current returns, reinvesting 22% of profits supports about 2.9% a year of fundamental growth, too little to drive meaningful growth.","Margins are expanding (+1.5% trend).","Forward indicators: deferred revenue up 201%.","Capex runs 1.6x depreciation (5.5% of sales), so it is building capacity for future growth.","Its Rule of 40 score is 26, below the 40 that marks a healthy growth business."],"own":["Insiders hold little stock (0.9%), and institutions hold 92%.","Shareholder yield is a modest 1.0% (0.8% in buybacks and 0.3% in dividends).","The share count has shrunk 1.2% a year over five years, steadily raising each holder's stake."],"people":["With about 25,430 employees, each generates about $324K of revenue,